  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-15T16:19:11.342Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Recently I updated VRChat and instantly I noticed a few problems with this recent update. One handed movement had been removed..I don't get why this was removed but it helped me to still be able to move especially since I have very bad drift in one of my controllers but not since the update vrchat still thinks my other controller is on even when I take out the battery. Our(Specifically Quest Users) option to have the ability to make our MB size go up farther than 10MB has been taken away and this takes away the enjoyment out of seeing avatars that are a bit higher than 10MB and I feel as though we(Specifically Quest Users) have been limited enough but this new up has just screwed over not only me but my friends and people I come across that play vrchat on a Quest standalone headset. So for these two tools to be taken away has been so irritating and has taken the enjoyment out of vrchat for me.",
